# compiler, libtool, and linker output.  every Makefile under src/ has a
# clean target that removes this same set - see src/auths/Makefile and the
# roughly thirty module directories that mirror it - so these are build
# output everywhere below this directory and must never be tracked (#9678).
# none of these patterns has a leading slash, so each applies at any depth
# under src/, and one entry here covers all of the module, api, server,
# util, and cmdline directories.  do not repeat them in per-directory
# .gitignore files.
#
# .o/.lo/.la/.so and .libs/ are the unix libtool outputs.  .obj/.lib/.exp/
# .idb/.pdb/.manifest/.dll/.exe are what the windows nmake build writes
# instead - config_windows.mk sets OBJ=obj, LIBEXT=dll and EXE=.exe, so the
# same clean lines produce different names there.  .ii is preprocessor
# output some compilers leave behind.
#
# output only one directory produces is ignored by that directory's own
# .gitignore instead
*.o
*.obj
*.lo
*.la
*.so
*.dll
*.lib
*.exp
*.idb
*.pdb
*.manifest
*.ii
*.exe
.libs/
